  "source": "The Public Health Agency of Sweden",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of the population (16–84 years or 16 years and older) that smokes tobacco products daily, sometimes or previously smoked. Percentage reported by region, gender and years (4 year mean values). Response rate for the Swedish National Public Health Survey: 2004 (60,8 %), 2005 (60,3 %), 2006 (60,1 %), 2007 (57,5 %), 2008 (55,7 %), 2009 (52,1 %), 2010 (50,6 %), 2011 (49 %), 2012 (49,4 %), 2013 (48,8 %), 2014 (48,1 %), 2015 (48,8 %), 2016 (47,0 %), 2018 (42,1 %), 2020 (42,3 %), 2021 (44,1 %), 2022 (37,9 %), 2024 (39,4 %). From 2016, the survey is conducted every two years. In 2021, an extra round of the survey was conducted due to the ongoing corona pandemic."
